# React Frontend Conventions

## Settings & Configuration

All storage keys and default values live in `src/config/settings.js`. Never read from `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` directly in a component. The GitHub token is kept in `sessionStorage` only (via `getGithubToken` / `setGithubToken`); never persist it to `localStorage`. Always bind the token to the signed-in Cognito `sub` (`arc_github_token_subject`): clear it on sign-out, account deletion, and subject mismatch; pass `authSubject` when saving from Settings.

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
import { getEffectiveSettings, getGithubToken } from '../config/settings';

// ❌ BAD
const token = localStorage.getItem('arc_github_token');
```

Build-time configuration uses `import.meta.env.VITE_*`; Cognito settings live in `src/config/auth.js`.

## API Calls

All API interactions go through `src/utils/api.js`, which takes the Cognito access token from `useAuth()` and sends it as `Authorization: Bearer`. Components never call `fetch` directly.

## Component Patterns

- Functional components only
- Extract reusable markup into a dedicated component (e.g., `StepRow`)
- Props should be fully typed or at minimum documented with JSDoc

## CSS & Accessibility

- Touch targets must be ≥ 44 × 44 px
- Interactive elements need `aria-label` when text is absent (e.g., icon-only buttons)
- Media queries required: `max-width: 768px`, `max-width: 360px`, `prefers-reduced-motion`

## Error Handling

API errors must surface a user-visible message. Never silently swallow a rejected promise.

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
try {
  const result = await startSprintAnalysis(settings);
  setExecutionArn(result.executionArn);
} catch (err) {
  setError(err.message || 'An unexpected error occurred');
}
```
